 We can use this to have alternate inputs trigger the same motions in our brain. If you don’t have a D-pad, you can use the left joystick instead!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775584858081","neuronKeys":["[#ba0c8]"],"edgeStrings":["[#ba0c8]_#_[#96a82]","[#ba0c8]_#_[#ebf9f]"],"description":"Pressing forward will drive SpikerBot forward. Each SpikerBot is unique, so be sure to tune the synaptic weights for each motor to make sure it drives straight!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775584892896","neuronKeys":["[#4427f]","[#f6348]"],"edgeStrings":["[#4427f]_#_[#e64ef]","[#4427f]_#_[#ebf9f]","[#f6348]_#_[#4427f]"],"description":"Holding left on your joystick or D-pad will rotate spikerbot left.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775584915161","neuronKeys":["[#9ec0d]","[#3a782]"],"edgeStrings":["[#9ec0d]_#_[#3a782]","[#3a782]_#_[#763d2]","[#3a782]_#_[#96a82]"],"description":"Holding the right input will rotate SpikerBot to the right.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775584958556","neuronKeys":["[#e65e1]","[#7cfa9]"],"edgeStrings":["[#e65e1]_#_[#e64ef]","[#e65e1]_#_[#763d2]","[#e65e1]_#_[#145eb]","[#e65e1]_#_[#5a5cd]","[#7cfa9]_#_[#e65e1]"],"description":"Holding hown, will reverse both wheels, and drive backwards while beeping and showing the brake lights.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775585000246","neuronKeys":["[#4427f]","[#ba0c8]"],"edgeStrings":["[#4427f]_#_[#ebf9f]","[#4427f]_#_[#e64ef]","[#ba0c8]_#_[#96a82]","[#ba0c8]_#_[#ebf9f]"],"description":"Holding two directions at once can make a banked turn. You can drive SpikerBot by only using one hand!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775585046629","neuronKeys":["[#cf45c]"],"edgeStrings":["[#cf45c]_#_[#145eb]"],"description":"Turn on SpikerBot’s headlights with the left bumper button L1, or assign the neuron to use a different input.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775585105598","neuronKeys":["[#0c639]"],"edgeStrings":["[#0c639]_#_[#145eb]","[#0c639]_#_[#5a5cd]"],"description":"Pressing the left trigger (L2) will blink the lights blue, and beep SpikerBot’s horn.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775585199743","neuronKeys":["[#7cfa9]","[#f6348]","[#21721]","[#9ec0d]"],"edgeStrings":[],"description":"What alterate controls would you use to drive SpikerBot? You can also use a bluetooth keyboard, or the keyboard on your computer if using the app there.","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Simple Gamepad Controlled Car","description":"Use a bluetooth gamepad to drive SpikerBot like a car and beep its horn! Works with a joystick or a D-pad.","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T15:56:58.988389"}}